  "reason": "Evidence: multiprofile with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms singleprofile (config_001, acc=0.485), confirming that multi-profile representation is a major design lever for RNA. However, we have no evidence yet about whether the aggregation method (avgpool vs. transformer) matters, which is a critical architectural choice that will affect all future multimodal configurations. Question tested: Does a transformer-based aggregation of multiple profiles yield meaningfully better performance than simple average pooling, holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (multiprofile) constant? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable extension of our current best result, so any performance difference is directly attributable to the aggregation method. Resolving this question before scaling to multimodal or alternative encoders ensures we build subsequent experiments on the correct aggregation backbone, maximizing information gained per experiment under a limited budget."
}

